  "constitutionalAuthorityStatementText": "<pre>\n[Congressional Record Volume 171, Number 1 (Friday, January 3, 2025)]\n[House]\nFrom the Congressional Record Online through the Government Publishing Office [<a href=\"https://www.gpo.gov\">www.gpo.gov</a>]\nBy Mr. CARTER of Georgia:\nH.R. 25.\nCongress has the power to enact this legislation pursuant\nto the following:\nArticle I, Section 8 of the Constitution\nThe single subject of this legislation is:\nTo promote freedom, fairness, and economic opportunity by\nrepealing the income tax and other taxes, abolishing the\nInternal Revenue Service, and enacting a national sales tax\nto be administered primarily by the States.\n[Page H36]\n</pre>",
